# UI Kit consumption

Every service frontend (`identity`, `webonone-v2`, `media`, `email`, and future `*/frontend`) must use **`@webonone/ui-kit`** for interactive UI — not raw HTML controls, not third-party component libraries, and not local copies of kit primitives.

Related: [ui-kit-project.mdc](ui-kit-project.mdc) (package/build), [feature-page-layout.mdc](feature-page-layout.mdc), [dialog-windows.mdc](dialog-windows.mdc), [form-creation skill](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md), [item-list skill](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md).

## Dependency and wiring

| Requirement | Where |
|-------------|-------|
| `"@webonone/ui-kit": "*"` in dependencies | `<service>/frontend/package.json` |
| Vite aliases: `@webonone/ui-kit`, `/styles`, `/tailwind` | `<service>/frontend/vite.config.ts` |
| `import '@webonone/ui-kit/styles'` in entry | `<service>/frontend/src/main.tsx` |
| `build:ui-kit` chained before frontend build | `<service>/package.json` |

See [microservice-architecture.mdc](microservice-architecture.mdc) for production `dist/` build order.

## Forbidden

- Raw HTML `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>` for interactive UI
- Third-party component libraries (MUI, Ant Design, Chakra, etc.)
- Copying kit source into `features/` or re-implementing kit primitives locally
- Page-level loading as plain text (`<p>Loading…</p>`) — use `Spinner` instead
- `Input` with `type="date"` — use `DatePicker` (native browser date UI is inconsistent and misaligns with other controls)

## Required component mapping

| UI need | Use from `@webonone/ui-kit` | Authoritative rule/skill |
|---------|----------------------------|--------------------------|
| App chrome | `AppShell`, `PageShell`, `AuthLayout`, `BrandLogo` | [platform-shell-navigation.mdc](platform-shell-navigation.mdc) |
| Feature pages | `FeaturePage`, `PageHeader` | [feature-page-layout.mdc](feature-page-layout.mdc) |
| Forms | `Form`, `FormField`, `Input`, `mapZodIssuesToFieldErrors` | [form-creation skill](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md) |
| Date fields | `DatePicker` (prefer `withIcon`) inside `FormField` | [form-creation skill](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md) |
| Lists | `ItemList`, `ItemListMenu`, `DropdownMenuItem` | [item-list skill](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md) |
| Modals | `CustomDialog`, `AlertDialog` | [dialog-windows.mdc](dialog-windows.mdc) |
| Page/section loading | `Spinner` (`size="lg"` for full section; `size="sm"` inside `Button`) | This rule |
| Errors | `Alert`, `AlertDescription` | This rule |
| Success feedback | `Alert` or `useToast` / `ToastProvider` | This rule |

When the kit lacks a component, extend ui-kit via [ui-kit-agent](../agents/ui-kit-agent.md) first — do not add a parallel primitive in a service.

## Allowed exceptions

- Domain preview: `<iframe sandbox srcDoc={…}>` for email/HTML previews
- Semantic copy: `<p>` for list metadata, pagination text, descriptions inside `ItemListContent`
- Routing shells (`router.tsx`, `PrivateRoute`) — no UI primitives needed
- `lucide-react` icons in nav config only (paired with ui-kit shell)

